# Gitleaks allowlist — known false positives (format: <commit>:<file>:<rule>:<line>).
#
# Prefer inline `# gitleaks:allow` comments on the fixture line itself: the
# push gate runs with `--log-opts=-1`, so a commit-scoped fingerprint goes
# stale the moment anyone edits the line, and every later push touching that
# file turns red again.
#
# Fingerprints below are kept only for commits already in history. They are
# not redundant with the inline allows: the nightly run walks the whole log,
# and an inline allow added today cannot retroactively cover the revision
# that introduced the fixture. So both mechanisms are needed — inline allows
# keep the push gate honest, fingerprints keep the nightly run honest. Adding
# a fixture means adding an inline allow; a nightly failure means adding a
# fingerprint for the old blob (the run prints the exact one to paste).
#
# tests/e2e/rm-rss-test.sh: the "secret" is a hardcoded JWT signing key for a
# throwaway local control-plane instance the RSS e2e script boots on
# 127.0.0.1:7812 — a test fixture, never a real credential.
